<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Third Taifa of Valencia</h1><p class="st-meta">1229 CE – 1238 CE · capital Valencia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Muslim kingdom of Valencia under Zayyan ibn Mardanish, which fell to James I of Aragon in 1238.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1229 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayyan-ibn-mardanish">Zayyan ibn Mardanish</a>, a descendant of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-mardanish">Wolf King</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-taifa-of-murcia">Second Taifa of Murcia</a>, overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-zayd-almohad-governor-of-valencia">Abu Zayd</a>. Abu Zayd fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a>, later converting to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and helping his campaigns.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Zayyan ruled the city and the irrigated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">huerta</a> with its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, seeking help from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hafsid-sultanate">Hafsids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>. His position was weak: he faced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-hud">Ibn Hud's</a> rival power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> and the steady advance of Aragonese forces, which won at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-puig">Puig</a> in 1237.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After a siege, Zayyan surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> to James I on 28 September 1238, and the Muslim population was allowed to leave. The city became the capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-valencia">Kingdom of Valencia</a>. Zayyan withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denia">Dénia</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1229 CE – 1238 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.16%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1229 CE – 1238 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Valencia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zayyan ibn Mardanish</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Valencia of Zayyan ibn Mardanish</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1234&amp;focus=third-taifa-of-valencia" aria-label="Third Taifa of Valencia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4671 764 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Third Taifa of Valencia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4991 1020L4794 1282M4991 1020L4984 945M4991 1020L4991 1020"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4794 1282h0M4984 945h0M4991 1020h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4991 1020h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4991 1020h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Valencia. <a href="/atlas?year=1234&amp;focus=third-taifa-of-valencia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
